<!--
  Traditional Chinese (繁體中文).

  A script-qualified folder (`b+zh+Hant`), not `values-zh-rTW`: the request is
  for the *script*, and one folder then covers every Traditional Chinese region
  (Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macau) instead of Taiwan alone. A device set to
  zh-Hant-TW, zh-Hant-HK or zh-Hant-MO all resolve here.

  Terminology follows what these platforms already use in Taiwan, so nothing
  reads as a literal translation of the English:
    mirror   = 鏡像      (Apple/Google Taiwan)
    cast     = 投放      (Google Home)
    network  = 網路      (Taiwan; 網絡 is Hong Kong)
    settings = 設定
    video    = 視訊 for the stream (視訊金鑰, 視訊編碼器),
               影片 for a clip or its URL (影片網址)
    Home     = 「家庭」  (Apple's Home app, whose members a receiver may be
                          restricted to)
  Product and protocol names (AirPlay, Wi-Fi, Android, GitHub, APK, HLS, mDNS,
  VPN, PIN, FairPlay, HomeKit, `main`, `nightly`) stay in Latin script.

  The error strings that end in a placeholder after a colon or in parentheses
  get the protocol's own explanation there: an exception's message, or the
  receiver's reason for ending a session. It is technical and English in every
  language, so only the sentence around it is translated here.
-->
